    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258-a2">

                <pb facs="0506" n="458" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg458"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    120.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Corvo to Mr. Moran.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Direction of Consulates and Commercial Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1877-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 10, 1877</date>. (Received January
                    15.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>In answer to a note which your excellency addressed me on the 19th December last
                    past, relative to the desirability of determinating telegraphically from Paris
                    the longitudes of both coasts of South America, and desiring the co-operation of
                    the Portuguese authorities to that end, I have the pleasure to inform your
                    excellency that the government of His Most Faithful Majesty feels disposed to
                    accede to the request of which your excellency is the interpreter, and that
                    necessary orders have and shall be given to that effect. Foreign Office, January
                    10, 1877.</p>
                <closer><signed>JOÃO DE ANDRADE CORVO.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Senhor <hi rendition="#small-caps">Benjamin Moran</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
